You're on the main square of Mech-City. People like ants bustle about, going on their errands. You can get to many interesting places from there - the most important is not to miss approach time.
On the western edge of the square you can see the house of famous Mech-City huntsman Beobras Beowulf, your friend Conan's father. You can drop by, if you want, Conan will certainly wish to come with you. The Library is to the northwest. You can look there for something interesting, that can prove useful. To the northeast there is the house of the inventor Nikolas Swift, your friend Doyle's father. Doyle is probably home, because he likes to stay in father's workshop. They say, knowledge is power, maybe it's wise to invite him with you. The house of traveler Cyrus Paganel is on the eastern edge of the square. He personally visited Wild Island once, and can tell you something that is not written in Doyle's books. You can go home for a while, or you can go to the place Wild Island is expected, and just wait for approaching. It's up to you.